{# Java Spring DI Configuration template — emits
src/main/java/org/prebid/server/spring/config/bidder/{Bidder}Configuration.java

Inputs:
  ctx.bidder_name              : str  — Java YAML name (lowercase, used for Spring property keys)
  ctx.bidder_class_root        : str  — PascalCase (e.g., "Kobler", "AdkernelAdn")
  ctx.uses_currency_conversion : bool — source spec's currency_conversion.used
  ctx.has_typed_config_props   : bool — Rule 35 fired (typed config subclass exists);
                                         when true, configurationProperties() returns the subclass
                                         and bidderCreator passes the subclass-typed config in.
  ctx.typed_config_class_name  : str|null — subclass name when has_typed_config_props.
                                         MUST be "{Bidder}ConfigurationProperties" (e.g.
                                         "KoblerConfigurationProperties"). NOT
                                         "{Bidder}BidderConfigurationProperties": that suffix belongs
                                         to the framework's own model/BidderConfigurationProperties
                                         and model/DefaultBidderConfigurationProperties, and no
                                         bidder upstream uses it.
  ctx.typed_fields             : list[dict]|null — the subclass's fields when has_typed_config_props;
                                         each: java_name, java_type, validation_annotations (list|null),
                                         notes (str|null), default_value (str|null). The subclass is
                                         emitted NESTED in this file -- see the shape note below.
  ctx.typed_config_javadoc     : str|null — Javadoc summary on the nested subclass
  ctx.typed_config_constraint_imports : list[str]|null — jakarta.validation.constraints.* imports
                                         needed by typed_fields' annotations, alphabetically
                                         sorted. Emitted in the bottom java/jakarta group per
                                         upstream ImportOrder.
  ctx.extra_constructor_args   : list[dict]|null — per-bidder extra constructor args; each:
      java_type    : str  — "CurrencyConversionService", custom service type, etc.
      java_name    : str  — argument name as referenced inside bidderCreator lambda
      bean_param   : str  — full Spring annotation form (e.g., "CurrencyConversionService currencyConversionService")
      lambda_arg   : str  — what the bidderCreator lambda passes through (e.g., "currencyConversionService")
  ctx.bidder_creator_extra_args: str|null — additional comma-separated args for the bidderCreator's `new {Bidder}Bidder(...)` call beyond `config.getEndpoint(), mapper`
  ctx.typed_config_lambda_getters: list[str]|null — names of TYPED (subclass) properties the
                                              bidderCreator must read, e.g. ["devEndpoint"].
                                              Each is emitted as `config.get<Name>()` in the
                                              lambda AND forces the explicit type witness on
                                              forBidder, because without it CFG infers to
                                              BidderConfigurationProperties and the getter does
                                              not resolve. Requires has_typed_config_props.
                                              Upstream canon: AdnuntiusBidderConfiguration
                                              (getEuEndpoint), KoblerConfiguration
                                              (getDevEndpoint).
  ctx.user_sync                : dict|null — user-sync configuration. Declared in bidder-config YAML ONLY.
                                              The Configuration class takes no usersync argument: BidderDepsAssembler
                                              derives the Usersyncer internally from the bound properties
                                              (`UsersyncerUtil.create`). Upstream deleted `UsersyncerCreator` in
                                              2880782f (#4464, 2026-07-09); emitting it does not compile.
                                              Canonical shape with usersync present: AdprimeConfiguration.java.
  ctx.endpoint_external_url_macro : bool — endpoint template contains the {PREBID_SERVER_ENDPOINT} macro, so the
                                              bean needs `@NotBlank @Value("${external-url}") String externalUrl`
                                              to resolve it (canonical: AaxConfiguration.java; 4 of 255 upstream
                                              configs). Default false — usersync does NOT require this parameter.
                                              The `@NotBlank` here is decorative and is emitted anyway, because all
                                              4 upstream instances carry it and a port that drops it diverges from
                                              the file a reviewer will diff against. It does not enforce: parameter
                                              validation comes from MethodValidationPostProcessor, whose pointcut is
                                              the CLASS-annotation form of AnnotationMatchingPointcut, and these
                                              @Configuration classes are not @Validated. Do not "fix" it by adding
                                              @Validated to the class — that changes proxying for every @Bean method
                                              on it, and no upstream config does that.
  ctx.javadoc_summary          : str|null  — class-level Javadoc summary; null → no Javadoc

Canonical shape per references/java-artifact-shapes.md §9 (Adverxo "BidderConfiguration"
form vs Kobler "Configuration" form): both forms are accepted by upstream; this template
emits the "Configuration" form as default. Operator flag --bidder-configuration-form
(future) can switch to the BidderConfiguration form.

RULE 35 SHAPE — the typed config subclass is NESTED in this file, not a separate one.
All 16 Rule-35 subclasses at e3ffd57 are nested classes inside their {Bidder}Configuration
(Adnuntius, Aduptech, Appnexus, AudienceNetwork, Beachfront, Epsilon, HuaweiAds, Kobler,
Magnite, MinuteMedia, Msft, NextMillennium, Rediads, Smartadserver, TheTradeDesk,
TripleliftNative); 15 are `private static class` and none is a separate file. Regenerate:

  git grep -lP 'class \w+ConfigurationProperties extends BidderConfigurationProperties' \
    -- 'src/main/java/org/prebid/server/spring/config/bidder/*Configuration.java' | wc -l

Annotation order is uniform across all 16: [@Validated] @Data
@EqualsAndHashCode(callSuper = true) @NoArgsConstructor. @Validated is emitted only when a
typed field carries a jakarta constraint, which is exactly the upstream correlation (7 of
the 16 carry it, and every one of those has at least one constraint). It is redundant --
the parent BidderConfigurationProperties is itself @Validated and spring resolves the
annotation up the type hierarchy -- but emitting it on a constrained subclass matches the
house form. It goes on the CLASS, not on the @Bean factory method.

ImportOrder per upstream checkstyle.xml `groups="*,/^java|^jakarta/"`,
`separated=true`: the catch-all `*` group (org.*, com.*, lombok.*) comes FIRST,
then a blank line, then `java.*` + `jakarta.*` at the BOTTOM. This is inverted
from typical Java conventions.

The PropertySource @value path is hardcoded to classpath:/bidder-config/{bidder}.yaml
(the upstream convention; matches the bidder-config.yaml.j2 emission).

FORMS MEASURED across the 255 upstream {Bidder}Configuration.java files at e3ffd57. Kobler
is the atypical file on three of the four, so diffing this template against Kobler alone
will suggest changes that move it AWAY from the corpus:

  @ConfigurationProperties argument   literal "adapters.x"   255/255   (concatenation: 0)
  BidderDepsAssembler.forBidder       bare, no type witness  243/255
  bidderCreator lambda parameter      `config`               253/254   (Kobler uses `cfg`)
  bidderDeps first parameter name     {bidder}ConfigurationProperties  14/15  (Kobler: `config`)

The 243/255 bare figure is a population count, not a licence to omit the type witness.
`forBidder` is `<CFG extends BidderConfigurationProperties> BidderDepsAssembler<CFG>`, so
with no witness CFG infers to the BOUND and the bidderCreator's function parameter is a
plain BidderConfigurationProperties. Where the creator needs the subclass, the witness is
required for the file to compile at all.

Established by compiling the upstream tree at e3ffd57, not by pattern-matching it. Each of
the 12 witness-carrying configs was compiled unmodified (12/12 clean), then recompiled with
only `.<Props>` removed:

  witness removed -> compile fails    12/12   (Magnite 6 errors, the rest 1 each)
  witness added to a bare config       0/4    errors, baseline 0/4

So the witness is load-bearing everywhere upstream spells it, and harmless where upstream
does not -- omitting it below is a corpus-matching choice, emitting it is a correctness one.
Two failure spellings, both from the same inference:

  inline lambda     cannot find symbol: method getDevEndpoint()
                    location: variable cfg of type BidderConfigurationProperties
  hoisted Function  Function<XProps,Bidder<?>> cannot be converted to
                    Function<BidderConfigurationProperties,Bidder<?>>

Regex over these 255 files is the wrong instrument for the question and gave three different
answers on three attempts -- an inline-lambda matcher misses AudienceNetwork's hoisted
`Function<Props, Bidder<?>>` local, an annotated-field matcher misses Magnite's fields, and
counting reads off the bean parameter instead of the lambda parameter reverses the result
(all 4 bare configs read typed getters -- off the bean parameter, which needs no witness).
That is why ctx.typed_config_lambda_getters and the witness are emitted together below and
cannot be set independently.

Regenerate any of them with, e.g.:

  git grep -c -P '@ConfigurationProperties\("adapters\.[a-z]' \
    -- 'src/main/java/org/prebid/server/spring/config/bidder/*Configuration.java' | wc -l
#}
