{#
  Guard: has_typed_config_props and typed_fields must agree.

  With jinja's default Undefined, a missing `typed_fields` iterates as empty, so
  a caller that sets the flag and forgets the data used to render a subclass with
  an EMPTY body -- a Rule 35 class that binds no properties at all, which is the
  one thing Rule 35 exists to do. Silent and downstream-invisible.

  Calling an undefined name is the one construct that raises under default
  Undefined (rendering one merely yields ""), so the guard is written as a call
  and the name carries the diagnosis.
